docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R18.md:11:This review certifies that the Phase 2 event log substrate meets every spec invariant before Phase 3 (memory graph) begins. It confirms: all 20 event kinds are modeled and emitted by the right tool sites; storage is append-only and replayable; payload spillover, hashing, and content-addressed dedupe work end-to-end; reader queries are bounded and scope-safe; compaction is daemon-managed with a versioned, independently-readable snapshot format; the P99 ≤5ms hot-path budget is met with quantitative evidence. The review verdict gates Phase 3 — a failed review here means Phase 3 cannot start because its memory-provenance depends on a trustworthy event log.
