docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T46.md:12:This task ships the cross-job integration test suite that proves Phase 6's invariants hold when all consolidation pieces run together: proposals from every job type land in `consolidation_proposals` without silent writes, apply/reject decisions route through the runtime correctly, replay reconstructs the same memory state, the bounded queue drops with warnings on overflow, malformed LLM responses emit `ConsolidationFailed` events while leaving prior memory unchanged, and high-scope proposals reach the manual-review queue instead of auto-applying. Unit tests in T39–T45 cover each module in isolation; this task wires them end-to-end so the spec's Phase 6 DoD ("consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered") is demonstrably met.
