docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:37:2. In `consolidation/replay.rs`, define `pub struct ReplayDriver { event_reader, proposal_store, memory_store, llm_response_cache: HashMap<PromptHash, ResponseBytes> }` and `pub enum ReplayMode { FromGenesis, FromSnapshot { snapshot_id }, FromEventId(EventId) }`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:38:3. Implement `ReplayDriver::replay(mode) -> ReplayReport`: (a) reset memory state to the snapshot's baseline (or empty if `FromGenesis`), (b) iterate `MemoryConsolidated` / `ConsolidationFailed` events in `event_id` order, (c) for each `MemoryConsolidated`, re-apply `proposed_state` from the embedded payload — do NOT re-call deterministic scanners or LLM drivers; replay is data-replay, not job-replay, (d) verify the resulting memory state hashes match the post-event hash recorded at original apply time (record-and-verify).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:39:4. Implement `ReplayDriver::reverse(proposal_id) -> Result<(), ReverseError>` for proposal reversal: read `prior_state` from `consolidation_proposals`, write it back through the memory store, emit a `MemoryConsolidated` event with `proposed_state = prior_state` and `prior_state = proposed_state` (the reverse delta), flip the proposal's `decision` to `reverted`. Reversal must be atomic: either all writes commit or none. Add a `reverted` variant to `ProposalDecision` (extend the T39 enum) and the matching migration.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:42:7. Make every applied proposal include `post_apply_state_hash: [u8; 32]` in its `MemoryConsolidated` payload so replay can detect divergence. Update `events::kinds::MemoryConsolidatedPayload` accordingly and bump its serde version handling per Phase 2 conventions.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:43:8. In `consolidation/replay_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) `replay(FromGenesis)` on a fixture with 50 mixed deterministic + LLM proposals reconstructs the same memory state byte-for-byte (state hash match), (b) reversal of a `Refresh` proposal restores `last_verified_at` exactly, (c) reversal of a `Supersede` proposal flips status back and clears the `memory_links` edge, (d) replay with no LLM driver available succeeds when provenance cache is populated and fails cleanly when it is not, (e) replay never calls the live `LlmDriver` (assert via a fake driver whose `complete` panics — replay must never invoke it), (f) reversal is idempotent: reverting an already-reverted proposal is a typed `AlreadyReverted` outcome, not a panic.
