docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:12:This task implements the deterministic consolidation jobs spec §Consolidation Engine names verbatim: duplicate detection, supersession-candidate proposals, demotion of unused/low-value memories, marking memories stale after graph changes, and refreshing memories whose evidence still matches. These jobs do not require LLM inference — they are computed entirely from the workspace graph, the memory graph, and `memory_accesses` / `memory_scores` from Phase 3. Each job MUST route through the T39 proposal runtime (no silent writes) and MUST run cheaply enough to be invoked from background scheduling without blocking. Together these jobs supply the "self-cleaning" half of consolidation that has to be online before the LLM-driven jobs (T42) layer on.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:20:> Phase 6 DoD: "consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered".
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:24:- Dependency outputs: T39 — `ConsolidationProposal`, `ProposalKind`, `BoundedJobQueue`, `consolidation_jobs` schema. Every deterministic job in this task emits proposals through T39.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:35:1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine "Consolidation jobs" list. Copy the verbatim names into module doc comments so each file states which spec bullet it implements.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:36:2. In `consolidation/duplicates.rs`, implement `DuplicateDetector::scan(workspace_id, kind_filter)` that buckets memories of the same `MemoryClass` and scope, computes pairwise vector similarity above a configurable threshold (default 0.92), confirms typed-evidence overlap (shared `FileId`/`SymbolId`), and emits an `UpdateMemory` or `Supersede` proposal pairing the older memory as supersedee of the newer when both carry compatible assertions, or a `Demote` proposal when both look stale. The detector must run in O(n log n) using vector-index nearest-neighbor queries, never full pairwise.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:37:3. In `consolidation/supersession.rs`, implement `SupersessionCandidates::scan(workspace_id)` that finds memories whose evidence has been replaced by newer memories on overlapping anchors. Emit a `Supersede` proposal: `prior_state` captures the older memory verbatim; `proposed_state` flips it to status `superseded` with a link back to the newer memory in the `memory_links` table.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:38:4. In `consolidation/demotion.rs`, implement `DemotionScanner::scan(workspace_id, cutoff)` that queries `memory_accesses` for memories with `access_count == 0` since `cutoff` AND `memory_scores.usefulness < demotion_threshold`. Emit a `Demote` proposal whose `proposed_state` lowers the memory's salience score and flips status to `unverified` if currently `verified`. Never delete: the spec invariant is reversibility.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:39:5. Add `consolidation/stale_marker.rs` (extending `mod.rs`) implementing `StaleMarker::on_graph_change(changed_files: Vec<FileId>)`: for every memory whose evidence cites any changed file or contained symbol, emit a `MarkStale` proposal that flips `verification_status` to `stale` and records `staleness_reason` in `prior_state` vs `proposed_state`. Wire it into the indexer's "files-updated" hook so it fires on graph deltas.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:40:6. Add `consolidation/refresh.rs` implementing `RefreshScanner::scan(workspace_id)`: for every memory whose evidence still resolves cleanly against the current graph AND whose `last_verified_at < refresh_interval`, emit a `Refresh` proposal whose `proposed_state` bumps `last_verified_at` to `now` without changing the assertion. This is the "refresh memories whose evidence still matches current code" spec bullet.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:41:7. Each scanner exposes the same shape: `scan(...) -> ScanReport { proposals_enqueued: u32, skipped: u32, elapsed: Duration }`. Every proposal carries `prior_state` and `proposed_state` so apply/reject is reversible.
