docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T40.md:12:This task adds the `synchronous post-task consolidation` mode from spec §Consolidation Engine. It runs only on small task traces immediately after a workflow concludes, producing an episode-summary proposal that links the task's event slice to a new or updated episode memory. It must NOT run on the hot path: spec §Phase 2 DoD pins event writes at ≤5ms P99 on `prepare_change` / `get_context_capsule`, and the consolidation engine §LLM-driven block forbids LLM inference on the synchronous post-task hot path. The session consolidator therefore uses the deterministic episode template only; LLM-driven episode generation lives in T42.
